

/*!
   \page index.html

	\title ESToolkit User Manual

   \indexpage ESToolkit User Manual
   \startpage ESToolkit User Manual

	The Elysian Shadows Toolkit or "ESTk" is a multiplatform
	game development environment facilitating the creation
	of the "next generation" of 2D games. Originally developed
	solely to power Elysian Shadows, it features a full-fledged
	dynamic lighting engine, pixel perfect shadows, 3D positional
	audio, 3D rigid body and particle physics, and is fully
	extensible through an extremely powerful Lua API.

	ESTk currently supports the following platforms:

	\list
	\li \l Windows
	\li \l MacOS X
	\li \l Linux
	\li \l iOS
	\li \l Android
	\li \l OUYA
	\li \l Sega Dreamcast
	\endlist

	Table of contents:

	\list
	\li \l {Getting Started}
	\li \l {Project Structure}
	\li \l {Creating Maps}
	\li \l {Creating Entities}
	\li \l {Dynamic Lighting}
	\li \l {Spine Integration}
	\li \l {Rigid Bodies}
	\li \l {Positional Audio}
	\li \l {Cross-platform Deployment}
	\li \l {Debugging and Troubleshooting}
	\li \l {Editor Tools}
	\li \l {Sheet Manager}
	\li \l {Lua API Reference}
	\endlist
*/


